  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe contributor asked for this: PathPilot Hub simulates Tormach's lathes, and CamCraft shipped only a generic `lathe.mch`. This adds two shipped lathe machines from **Tormach's operator manuals**, which the contributor supplied:\n\n| | Tormach 8L (UM10753 §3.1) | Tormach 15L Slant-PRO (UM10225 §1.1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| X / Z stroke | 4.5\" / 10\" | 10\" / 12\" |\n| Spindle | 180-2500 / 350-5000 rpm (two ranges, 5C) | 180-2500 rpm (6\" chuck) |\n| Feed / rapid | 150 IPM | 60 IPM |\n| Power | 1.1 kW (1.5 hp, Tormach web; the manual states none) | 2.24 kW (3 hp continuous) |\n| Tools | 99 (gang / QCTP, PathPilot tool table) | 8 (8-position turret) |\n\n- **Conventions:** both machines are inch, `kind: lathe`, with the full stroke either way of the work zero, like the shipped Tormach mills.\n- **Conservative choices:**\n  - **8L X is 4.5\":** the manual settles it. Tormach's web knowledge base says 10\", which is the 15L's figure.\n  - **15L top speed is 2500 rpm,** the default chuck's rating. A shop on the 5C collet (250-3500 rpm) can raise it in its own copy.\n- **Test updates:** the shipped-machine expectation list (`machine.rs`) names both lathes. The Tormach Z0 safe-retract law (`tormach_safe_retract.rs`) is a mill-post law, so it skips lathes; they retract on their own post (#612).\n- **Not included:** the 15LX (#619) and the M+ mills (#618) follow separately.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/611-tormach-lathes.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/tormach_lathes.rs`, 2/2:** every lathe states its manual's figures (travel, feed, rpm and ranges, power, tool count, kind lathe, inch, no Y). The lathes are never offered as mills.\n- **Machine suites:** machine 32, machine_library 11, tormach_machines 5, tormach_safe_retract 4.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the app suites are green after this fix (the first run caught the two machine-list tests). conformance 6, posting 17, lathe_post 7, turning_thread 8.\n- **`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`:** clean.\n- No golden or snapshot changed. Fork synced at v0.16.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA Hub run on the 8L or 15L. Until #612 (the PathPilot lathe post) lands, these machines judge envelope, rpm and feed, but the default lathe post writes Fanuc dialect, which PathPilot won't run.\n\nChangelog: Tormach 8L and 15L Slant-PRO ship as lathe machines, from Tormach's operator manuals (#611)\n\nFixes #611\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
